%% Part 3 modified sequence with data access. Author: Thin Lei Sandi (523K0075).
sequenceDiagram
    title UC2 · Confirm or Reject an Incoming Order · Thin Lei Sandi (523K0075)
    actor Staff as Kitchen Staff
    participant UI as Kitchen View
    participant HTTP as Kitchen HTTP Controller
    participant Service as Kitchen Service
    participant Repo as Kitchen Repository
    participant DB as SQLite
    participant Notify as Notification Simulator

    Staff->>UI: Open incoming orders
    UI->>HTTP: GET /api/kitchen/orders
    HTTP->>Service: Resolve staff and retrieve assigned-hub queue
    Service->>Repo: Read staff role, hub and Submitted orders
    Repo->>DB: SELECT users, hubs, orders and item quantities
    Repo-->>Service: Staff and queue records
    Service->>Service: Enforce kitchen role and assigned hub
    alt Unauthorized
        Service-->>HTTP: Access denied
        HTTP-->>UI: 403 without queue data
    else Authorized
        Service-->>HTTP: Assigned-hub queue
        HTTP-->>UI: 200 queue or empty list
        UI-->>Staff: Display orders or no incoming orders
    end

    opt Staff selects an order
        Staff->>UI: Review order
        UI->>HTTP: GET /api/kitchen/orders/id
        HTTP->>Service: details(username, id)
        Service->>Repo: Read staff and order/payment snapshot
        Repo->>DB: SELECT user, order, hub and payment
        Repo-->>Service: Current records
        Service->>Service: Check role, ID, existence, hub and Submitted status
        alt Review denied or order unavailable
            Service-->>HTTP: Domain error
            HTTP-->>UI: 400, 403, 404 or 409 without changes
        else Review permitted
            Service->>Repo: Read item snapshots
            Repo->>DB: SELECT order_items
            Repo-->>Service: Items, quantities and saved prices
            Service-->>HTTP: Review details
            HTTP-->>UI: 200 order details
        end
    end

    opt Staff submits a decision
        Staff->>UI: Confirm or Reject with reason
        UI->>HTTP: POST /api/kitchen/orders/id/decision
        Note over HTTP,Service: Access and JSON checks precede decide. Invalid requests return without writes.
        HTTP->>Service: decide(username, id, input)
        Service->>Repo: Run decision transaction
        Repo->>DB: BEGIN IMMEDIATE
        Service->>Repo: Re-read staff, hub and order
        Repo->>DB: SELECT current staff and order
        Repo-->>Service: Current records
        Service->>Service: Recheck authorization, ownership and Submitted status
        Service->>Service: Validate decision and required rejection reason
        alt Validation or database write fails
            Note over Service,DB: Any failed check or write aborts the transaction
            Repo->>DB: ROLLBACK
            Service-->>HTTP: Domain error or storage failure
            HTTP-->>UI: 400, 403, 404, 409, 422 or 500 without partial changes
        else Checks and writes succeed
            Service->>Repo: Record decision and read saved result
            Repo->>DB: UPDATE orders only while Submitted
            Repo->>DB: INSERT order_decisions with staff, time and reason
            Repo->>DB: INSERT customer_notifications with failed flag
            Repo->>DB: SELECT saved decision and notification
            Repo-->>Service: Saved result inside transaction
            Repo->>DB: COMMIT
            Service->>Notify: Attempt simulated customer notification after commit
            alt Simulator returns sent or failed
                Notify-->>Service: Outcome
                Service->>Repo: Record notification outcome
                Repo->>DB: UPDATE notification status and attempted time
            else Notification attempt or outcome update throws
                Note over Service,DB: Keep committed decision and durable failed notification flag
            end
            Service-->>HTTP: Saved decision and notification outcome
            HTTP-->>UI: 200 confirmation or rejection result
            UI-->>Staff: Display status, staff, timestamp and applicable reason
            Note over UI,DB: Refreshing the queue excludes this order. Order and payment history remain.
        end
    end
    Note over Service,DB: UC1 receipt refresh checks owner and checkout reference before reading the latest decision.
